{"name":"Perfect Dark","hex":"#313390","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"perfect","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Fitting its definition precisely.","Having all of its parts in harmony with a common purpose."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The perfect tense, or a form in that tense.","A perfect score; the achievement of finishing a stage or task with no mistakes."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/perfect"},{"term":"dark","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having an absolute or (more often) relative lack of light.","Extinguished."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A complete or (more often) partial absence of light.","Ignorance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dark"}],"entries":[{"title":"Perfect Dark","blocks":[{"text":"Perfect Dark is a 2000 first-person shooter game developed and published by Rare for the Nintendo 64. The first game of the Perfect Dark series, it follows Joanna Dark, an agent of the Carrington Institute research centre, as she attempts to stop an extraterrestrial conspiracy by rival corporation dataDyne. The game features a campaign mode where the player must complete a series of levels to progress through the story, as well as a range of multiplayer options, including a co-operative mode and traditional deathmatch settings with computer-controlled bots."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/32/Perfect_dark_box.jpg/330px-Perfect_dark_box.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Perfect_Dark","wikidata":"Q1408723"},{"title":"Perfect Dark (P2P)","blocks":[{"text":"Perfect Dark (パーフェクトダーク) is a peer-to-peer file-sharing (P2P) application from Japan designed for use with Microsoft Windows. It was launched in 2006. Its author is known by the pseudonym Kaichō . Perfect Dark was developed with the intention for it to be the successor to both Winny and Share software. While Japan's Association for Copyright of Computer Software reported that in January 2014, the number of nodes connected on Perfect Dark was less than on Share, but more than on Winny, Netagent in 2018 reported Winny being the largest with 50 000 nodes followed by Perfect Dark with 30 000 nodes followed by Share with 10 000. Netagent asserts that the number of nodes on Perfect Dark have fallen since 2015 while the numbers of Winny hold steady. Netagent reports that users of Perfect Dark are most likely to share books/manga."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b7/Perfect_Dark_%28%E3%82%BD%E3%83%95%E3%83%88%E3%82%A6%E3%82%A7%E3%82%A2%29_%E3%82%A2%E3%82%A4%E3%82%B3%E3%83%B3.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Perfect_Dark_(P2P)","wikidata":"Q1734019"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/32/Perfect_dark_box.jpg/330px-Perfect_dark_box.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/32/Perfect_dark_box.jpg/330px-Perfect_dark_box.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APerfect_dark_box.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/af/Perfect_Dark_Gameplay.jpg/330px-Perfect_Dark_Gameplay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/af/Perfect_Dark_Gameplay.jpg/330px-Perfect_Dark_Gameplay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"In this level, the player is aiming at an opponent. The game's HUD at the bottom right corner shows the player's remaining ammunition and the weapon's selected function.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APerfect_Dark_Gameplay.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Nintendo-64-Memory-Expansion-Pak.jpg/500px-Nintendo-64-Memory-Expansion-Pak.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Nintendo-64-Memory-Expansion-Pak.jpg/1280px-Nintendo-64-Memory-Expansion-Pak.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Nintendo-64-Memory-Expansion-Pak.jpg/500px-Nintendo-64-Memory-Expansion-Pak.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Expansion Pak is required to access the game's campaign and most of the multiplayer features.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANintendo-64-Memory-Expansion-Pak.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c0/Perfect_Dark_Japanese_Ad.jpg/250px-Perfect_Dark_Japanese_Ad.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c0/Perfect_Dark_Japanese_Ad.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c0/Perfect_Dark_Japanese_Ad.jpg/250px-Perfect_Dark_Japanese_Ad.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"While the localised title of \"Red and Black\" was ultimately dropped, Japanese advertisements and box art still kept its dual colour theme.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APerfect_Dark_Japanese_Ad.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b7/Perfect_Dark_%28%E3%82%BD%E3%83%95%E3%83%88%E3%82%A6%E3%82%A7%E3%82%A2%29_%E3%82%A2%E3%82%A4%E3%82%B3%E3%83%B3.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b7/Perfect_Dark_%28%E3%82%BD%E3%83%95%E3%83%88%E3%82%A6%E3%82%A7%E3%82%A2%29_%E3%82%A2%E3%82%A4%E3%82%B3%E3%83%B3.p